WEBVTT

00:01:42.420 --> 00:01:49.260
You are a winner.

00:01:49.260 --> 00:01:52.590
Who remembers the price you paid?

00:01:52.590 --> 00:01:55.590
Who remembers the bitter days of the beginning?

00:01:55.590 --> 00:01:57.780
The friends who left.

00:01:57.780 --> 00:02:00.000
The ones who passed by your side.

00:02:01.020 --> 00:02:04.860
who lived next to you and carried in their souls,

00:02:04.980 --> 00:02:09.000
just like you, the ambition of triumphing.

00:03:01.210 --> 00:03:04.680
I met him through the cigar. I never thought I'd find him here.

00:03:04.880 --> 00:03:07.280
- I travel a lot, miss... - Liria Jimenez.

00:03:07.480 --> 00:03:11.410
- Nice to meet you. - On the other hand, this is my first trip.

00:03:11.610 --> 00:03:14.600
- Don't you know Buenos Aires? - I know it's wonderful.

00:03:14.800 --> 00:03:18.650
It's a great city, my city. But it can be very cruel.

00:03:18.850 --> 00:03:22.180
- Are you going for a walk? - I want to be an artist. I want to triumph.

00:03:22.380 --> 00:03:25.680
- In a movie? - No, I'm taking my songs.

00:03:25.880 --> 00:03:28.470
- Are you sure of your success? - Very sure.

00:03:28.670 --> 00:03:30.000
- Do you have family? - I don't know them.

00:03:31.630 --> 00:03:36.770
- Why don't you help me? - I'm not sure, but I'll make you listen to it on Belgrano Radio.

00:03:36.770 --> 00:03:40.810
- You don't see, luck is on my side. - Where are you going to live?

00:03:40.810 --> 00:03:48.150
- I'll look for a modest hotel. - I know a pension in the center, very close to Corrientes Street.

00:03:48.150 --> 00:03:51.760
- It belongs to the Sorellanas sisters. Did you hear about them? - They were singers.

00:03:51.760 --> 00:04:00.000
And very famous, until the bad years came. The eldest, Rosa Lester, is the least grumpy, however...

00:04:00.000 --> 00:04:03.340
Maria Blanca, with her screams and her nerves.

00:04:03.340 --> 00:04:06.680
- This coffee is more expensive than the other and it doesn't pay off. - But it's better.

00:04:06.680 --> 00:04:09.480
Better is the cheapest. Or do you think we'll find the money on the street?

00:04:09.480 --> 00:04:12.310
- Things will be fixed. - Everything will be fixed.

00:04:12.310 --> 00:04:14.820
It's not Borla who has to deal with the collectors.

00:04:14.820 --> 00:04:19.120
But since this goes on like this, we're going to end up asking for limosne.

00:04:19.120 --> 00:04:21.230
- Yes. - I put sugar in the sugar mill.

00:04:21.230 --> 00:04:24.860
Okay, of Rocha, no more. Eight terrones for four cups.

00:04:24.860 --> 00:04:27.780
- Do you have large lilies? - Lidia puts four.

00:04:27.780 --> 00:04:30.000
Because she's used to drinking it with less. Or if not,

00:04:30.000 --> 00:04:33.810
- How much for a cup of coffee? - It's almost ready, we're not machines.

00:04:33.810 --> 00:04:38.510
That fresh guy, three months behind and he still comes to ask for coffee.

00:04:38.510 --> 00:04:40.150
If he could, I'd give it to him.

00:04:40.150 --> 00:04:42.330
Poor thing, things don't go well for him.

00:04:42.330 --> 00:04:45.600
- Because he's moving out of the theater house. - Sister, he's a great actor.

00:04:45.600 --> 00:04:48.660
That's what he says, but he never went over the top.

00:04:48.660 --> 00:04:50.480
- Clarita. - Yes, miss?

00:04:50.480 --> 00:04:53.020
- Finish these dishes once and for all. - Yes, ma'am.

00:04:53.020 --> 00:04:57.750
- And don't break them, just break them. - I don't know why I don't send you back to Silo's.

00:04:57.750 --> 00:04:59.410
No, miss, that's not...

00:05:00.160 --> 00:05:03.430
I'll give it to you, take it. You must follow me to change the dining room.

00:05:03.430 --> 00:05:05.830
And be careful to put more than two pincers in each cup.

00:05:05.830 --> 00:05:10.280
In those days, theater was something else.

00:05:10.280 --> 00:05:11.650
What seasons!

00:05:11.650 --> 00:05:15.440
I remember that when I was the winner of Pablo's company...

00:05:15.440 --> 00:05:17.440
Who was Pablo? He was a young lady from Lidia.

00:05:17.440 --> 00:05:19.520
When he was called "Pablo" in the street,

00:05:19.520 --> 00:05:21.700
everyone knows that if you talk about Don Pablo, you can be...

00:05:21.700 --> 00:05:24.390
As I told you, once I went to the theater with a boy.

00:05:24.390 --> 00:05:26.720
From the entrance, I saw that he had something.

00:05:26.720 --> 00:05:30.000
And I got him a ticket. That boy's name was...

00:05:30.000 --> 00:05:32.640
His name was Riquel Serrano.

00:05:32.800 --> 00:05:34.370
What a time!

00:05:34.680 --> 00:05:37.280
Do you remember Don Porfirio and the coffee he paid Castro?

00:05:37.530 --> 00:05:39.530
- How many cups do you have? - Two.

00:05:39.730 --> 00:05:41.460
A lot of sugar relaxes the palate.

00:05:41.660 --> 00:05:44.120
I didn't put anything on Don Porfirio because it's bad for his diabetes.

00:05:44.320 --> 00:05:46.960
That was taught to you by Maria Blanca.

00:05:47.620 --> 00:05:50.480
- What do you do in the movies? - I always do.

00:05:50.780 --> 00:05:52.840
What happens is that no one takes you to the point in the studio.

00:05:53.040 --> 00:05:54.680
- And you think everything is very easy? - Yes, I know.

00:05:54.880 --> 00:05:57.970
The excuse of always, as you are attending to the sound, you can't talk to the director.

00:06:00.250 --> 00:06:01.950
I spent five days studying that paper.

00:06:01.970 --> 00:06:04.150
Zajoni studied his master's degree for eight years.

00:06:04.170 --> 00:06:06.670
- And what do you have to get into? - Just a comment.

00:06:06.690 --> 00:06:08.730
Comment on your own business, understand?

00:06:08.750 --> 00:06:10.410
It would be better if you paid what you owe.

00:06:10.430 --> 00:06:12.270
- You're going to shut up, Amanda! - I won't shut up!

00:06:12.290 --> 00:06:14.790
Or do I have to put up with this old loser?

00:06:14.850 --> 00:06:16.490
I'm fed up with everything, you know?

00:06:16.550 --> 00:06:17.830
Fed up with you!

00:06:17.850 --> 00:06:19.070
With all this tension!

00:06:19.090 --> 00:06:20.510
With all these people!

00:06:20.530 --> 00:06:22.630
Fed up with being an extra!

00:06:22.650 --> 00:06:23.780
I'm fed up!

00:06:34.000 --> 00:06:38.690
Listen to Don Portillo, they gave me a piece of paper and now I'm in trouble.

00:06:38.810 --> 00:06:40.340
They're things from the beginning.

00:06:40.640 --> 00:06:42.770
- What a scandal was that? - My wife...

00:06:42.870 --> 00:06:46.200
Your wife is better off in prison, otherwise she'll drive us all crazy.

00:06:47.440 --> 00:06:53.560
He spoke to Rastano.

00:06:53.600 --> 00:06:56.150
It seems they're going to get me to act in an audition.

00:06:56.300 --> 00:06:59.670
- It's a kind of test. - Rastano is very good.

00:07:00.250 --> 00:07:04.040
I met your father in the family. Do you remember, Mrs. Blanca?

00:07:04.040 --> 00:07:05.560
Yes, I remember.

00:07:05.560 --> 00:07:12.620
The old Frambron. He was a splendid, generous, fulfilling guy.

00:07:12.620 --> 00:07:17.530
By the way, I was looking at your accounts. They're a little late.

00:07:17.530 --> 00:07:22.110
I have a perspective, you know? Olinda is about to go on tour.

00:07:22.110 --> 00:07:24.110
She needs an important characteristic.

00:07:24.110 --> 00:07:27.080
With perspective you can't be the cook, Mr. Ramos.

00:07:27.080 --> 00:07:30.000
Have a little patience. You'll see, everything will be fine.

00:07:31.690 --> 00:07:33.630
I'll talk to Guipochea tomorrow.

00:07:33.630 --> 00:07:38.230
Now I don't have to represent her.

00:07:38.230 --> 00:07:40.870
This is another trip.

00:07:40.870 --> 00:07:43.350
I think it's a family matter.

00:07:43.350 --> 00:07:46.250
- What matter? - She might tell you that your children are waiting.

00:07:46.250 --> 00:07:49.380
- But I don't have children. - Neither does she.

00:07:49.380 --> 00:07:53.430
Come, tell me about the radio.

00:07:53.430 --> 00:07:55.270
Who is this?

00:07:55.270 --> 00:07:57.640
Someone who is about to arrive.

00:07:57.640 --> 00:08:00.000
A young man?

00:08:03.740 --> 00:08:06.240
Look, everything is a triumph for him.

00:08:06.810 --> 00:08:09.250
How bitter the road will be for him.

00:08:09.310 --> 00:08:10.790
Is that what the letters say?

00:08:10.810 --> 00:08:13.480
No, that's what life taught me.

00:08:15.390 --> 00:08:16.840
What a good boy he is.

00:08:17.420 --> 00:08:19.520
Too bad you never get it right.

00:08:20.840 --> 00:08:22.210
Go see who's calling.

00:08:38.440 --> 00:08:40.880
- Hi, actor. - Carlitos, my son?

00:08:40.880 --> 00:08:44.760
- I don't know if you saw who I am. - Don't get offended.

00:08:44.760 --> 00:08:49.330
A year ago I had a friend who was just like you, and his name was Carlitos.

00:08:49.330 --> 00:08:53.460
You are you, right? I mean, you are the Golden Horse.

00:08:53.460 --> 00:08:56.710
Tell me, Carlitos, is this the Orellana Pension or what?

00:08:56.710 --> 00:08:59.350
Yes, sir, the Orellana Pension, sister. Come in.

00:09:00.030 --> 00:09:01.920
- No, we needed more. - Thank you.

00:09:01.920 --> 00:09:07.650
- I'm Dr. Askoitian's recommender. - Oh, yes. We were expecting you tomorrow.

00:09:07.650 --> 00:09:11.950
- When will you bring the rest of the luggage? - It's all in the suitcase, and there's still plenty of space.

00:09:11.950 --> 00:09:15.490
- I don't know if they told you that you have to pay in advance. - Did they leave you many suitcases?

00:09:15.490 --> 00:09:19.790
- We already have 32. - So this is the piano.

00:09:19.790 --> 00:09:23.490
- A very good piano. - Askoitian told us that you are a pianist.

00:09:23.490 --> 00:09:27.770
- Yes, miss. Pianist and composer. - First of all, I'm going to ask you something.

00:09:27.770 --> 00:09:30.000
- You tell me. - Try not to get the inspiration...

00:09:30.000 --> 00:09:31.640
at the time people go to bed.

00:09:31.640 --> 00:09:34.350
- Our new hotel, sir. - Mariano Martínez.

00:09:34.350 --> 00:09:37.240
- We knew you had to come for the letters. - What letters?

00:09:37.240 --> 00:09:39.960
- I didn't write. - Mr. Martínez, allow me your documents.

00:09:39.960 --> 00:09:52.020
- Of course. - Yes, that's fine.

00:09:52.020 --> 00:09:53.940
- Do you want to wait a moment? - Of course.

00:09:53.940 --> 00:09:56.660
Excuse me.

00:10:06.750 --> 00:10:09.540
We're ready. We have music.

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:12.260
The noise that was missing in this house.

00:11:00.160 --> 00:11:03.510
Thank you. This is the first applause I receive.

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:05.790
- You'll receive a lot of applause. - I don't think so.

00:11:05.890 --> 00:11:08.310
- Very kind. - Miss Lilla is a famous singer.

00:11:08.410 --> 00:11:10.160
- Oh, really? - Don't listen to her.

00:11:10.220 --> 00:11:13.800
I'm in the kitchen. I could do an audition tomorrow.

00:11:13.900 --> 00:11:15.430
- It will be very good for you. - Thank you.

00:11:15.530 --> 00:11:18.440
Mr. Martínez, your room is ready. Do you want to see it?

00:11:18.490 --> 00:11:20.520
- Yes, miss. - Of course.

00:11:21.240 --> 00:11:23.080
- Good night, friend. - Good night.

00:11:23.180 --> 00:11:26.080
I'm going to the café to see if I can find Chino Palomero.

00:11:26.590 --> 00:11:28.640
- Good night. - Good night.

00:11:31.530 --> 00:11:34.790
Poor little man. He's so alone.

00:11:35.070 --> 00:11:37.010
Life is hard with him.

00:11:37.960 --> 00:11:39.600
Life is not easy for me.

00:11:40.210 --> 00:11:42.840
But he's so cute.

00:11:45.340 --> 00:11:48.560
Clarita, stop scaring the flies with your whispers and get on that van.

00:12:08.600 --> 00:12:10.400
- Do you know about the light? - Don't turn it on, Carlitos.

00:12:10.940 --> 00:12:17.540
Come here, look. Don't you think it's wonderful?

00:12:18.220 --> 00:12:20.200
- What? - What do you mean?

00:12:20.750 --> 00:12:22.540
- The Corrientes Street. - Oh!

00:12:23.600 --> 00:12:27.040
When someone's name is there, that someone is famous.

00:12:28.480 --> 00:12:30.000
Look how those lights shine.

00:12:30.990 --> 00:12:34.740
One day, I'll see my name on the street too.

00:12:37.200 --> 00:12:40.340
That street has a music, and I have to say it.

00:12:40.500 --> 00:12:44.050
When I was there, all the city sounds sounded like music to me.

00:12:44.200 --> 00:12:46.770
- Where is it? - Over there.

00:12:47.270 --> 00:12:49.750
It was taken by Mrs. Maria Blanca.

00:12:49.840 --> 00:12:51.990
Oh, you're in the asylum?

00:12:52.140 --> 00:12:55.220
Yes, I don't have anyone.

00:12:55.650 --> 00:12:59.190
You have me, I'm your friend.

00:13:00.090 --> 00:13:04.230
- A famous friend. - Not yet.

00:13:05.830 --> 00:13:09.410
It's not so easy to get out of a hardware store to get to success.

00:13:09.560 --> 00:13:14.100
- A hardware store? - My uncle's.

00:13:14.200 --> 00:13:16.570
I used to work there, in that hardware store.

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:23.010
- But you're going to get there. - He's a great boy, Carlitos.

00:13:23.770 --> 00:13:26.530
See you tomorrow, Mr. Martínez.

00:14:00.220 --> 00:14:03.680
My dear Francinatra, I almost forgot about you.

00:14:03.680 --> 00:14:19.400
It is what those who do not know how much bitterness the triumph costs.

00:14:30.380 --> 00:14:34.040
lights that yearn for those who ignore how life shatters.

00:14:34.040 --> 00:14:47.860
Street of success, street of tears, of pain, and of indifference.

00:14:48.690 --> 00:14:56.560
- Tomás, can you hear me? - Get out of the way.

00:14:56.560 --> 00:15:00.000
You have to get out of the way, because you're the only one who feels it.

00:15:01.690 --> 00:15:05.530
I'm poisoned by taking so many pills.

00:15:05.610 --> 00:15:08.730
- Shut up! - Calm down, Maria Blanca.

00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:11.820
How can I calm down? My head is bursting with worries.

00:15:11.900 --> 00:15:13.890
There are pensioners who don't pay.

00:15:13.970 --> 00:15:16.470
I couldn't sleep all night thinking about what I was reading.

00:15:16.550 --> 00:15:18.550
And when I get to sleep at dawn,

00:15:18.630 --> 00:15:20.790
that damned Sorsal starts to sing.

00:15:20.870 --> 00:15:22.950
Come here, Mocosa. It's about you.

00:15:23.030 --> 00:15:25.990
- Where is that bird? - There's no bird in the house.

00:15:26.230 --> 00:15:30.000
- There's no bird? - What happened to the house?

00:15:30.090 --> 00:15:31.870
- He woke me up. - Wasn't it a plane?

00:15:31.910 --> 00:15:36.370
- A plane? It was your sorsal. - No, miss, I let it go a long time ago.

00:15:36.410 --> 00:15:38.450
You let it go five times and it always comes back.

00:15:38.490 --> 00:15:40.190
Sorsal or messenger dove?

00:15:40.230 --> 00:15:41.750
- Now I'm going to my house. - Don't bother, miss.

00:15:41.790 --> 00:15:45.390
- I'll bring you the empty cage. - Sister.

00:15:46.130 --> 00:15:48.610
Sorsal is the only thing she has in her life.

00:15:48.650 --> 00:15:51.980
- You shouldn't have the birds as prisoners. - I like to hear them sing.

00:15:52.020 --> 00:15:54.640
Tell me, when we were the famous Orellana duo,

00:15:54.680 --> 00:15:57.450
would you have liked to be locked in a cage to hear us sing?

00:15:57.490 --> 00:16:00.000
- It should have been a parrot cage. - At least not so ugly.

00:16:00.000 --> 00:16:08.520
- But you thought this was the market. - I'll explain later.

00:16:08.520 --> 00:16:10.520
Explain it to me now. This is my room and not a henhouse.

00:16:10.520 --> 00:16:13.520
- Send me away with that bird. - Oh, no, hide me, poor Sinatra.

00:16:13.520 --> 00:16:16.520
- Mrs. Maria Blanca doesn't want him at home. - Excuse me, Carlitos.

00:16:16.520 --> 00:16:19.520
I don't want trouble with old women, birds or chiquilines.

00:16:19.520 --> 00:16:21.520
- Don't call him, let me hide him. - Clarita!

00:16:21.520 --> 00:16:23.920
- What are you doing? - Nothing.

00:16:23.920 --> 00:16:27.020
I was passing by and Mr. Martinez asked me to get his shoes...

00:16:27.020 --> 00:16:29.510
...because he can't find them.

00:16:38.120 --> 00:16:42.080
I'll walk down right away.

00:16:48.360 --> 00:16:51.110
That girl is from the asylums and she's under our custody.

00:16:51.230 --> 00:16:54.270
I'd appreciate it if you'd remember where you left your shoes...

00:16:54.400 --> 00:16:56.500
- ...because this is a very serious house. - But miss, don't...

00:16:56.600 --> 00:16:59.030
You can't get away alive, Mr. Martínez.

00:17:03.960 --> 00:17:08.180
- Martínez, your phone. - Downstairs.

00:17:10.620 --> 00:17:20.890
- A young lady named Lucía. - How are you, darling?

00:17:21.100 --> 00:17:23.810
- Is she your lover? - Get out of here, will you?

00:17:24.780 --> 00:17:27.550
I felt so bad not to see you last night.

00:17:27.710 --> 00:17:30.000
You know that if I didn't see you for a long time...

00:17:30.380 --> 00:17:32.500
- Where's the party? - Going to the party?

00:17:32.520 --> 00:17:34.500
- What luck! - Do you want to shut up?

00:17:35.170 --> 00:17:36.630
No, it's not you, dear.

00:17:37.420 --> 00:17:40.470
- We're having the meeting here. - Yes.

00:17:41.330 --> 00:17:43.990
- Leopoldo lends the house. - You're in everything.

00:17:44.080 --> 00:17:46.260
- Where is she? - Yes, no problem.

00:17:46.830 --> 00:17:50.230
- Until the night, dear. - You've known her for a long time?

00:17:50.430 --> 00:17:53.820
- And what do you care? - Leave that.

00:17:54.800 --> 00:17:57.080
- Hello. - What?

00:17:58.290 --> 00:18:00.000
Miss Lidia, call her over.

00:18:00.000 --> 00:18:01.340
Mr. Chávez Cruz is on the line.

00:18:01.340 --> 00:18:02.280
Yes, thank you.

00:18:02.280 --> 00:18:06.730
Hello?

00:18:06.730 --> 00:18:09.660
Yes.

00:18:09.660 --> 00:18:10.660
Yes, nice to meet you.

00:18:10.660 --> 00:18:12.030
Yes, how nice to meet you.

00:18:12.030 --> 00:18:13.150
Oh, thank you very much.

00:18:13.150 --> 00:18:17.230
Yes, of course, I'll be punctual.

00:18:17.230 --> 00:18:19.180
I have to go to Radio Belgrano.

00:18:19.180 --> 00:18:20.180
What?

00:18:20.180 --> 00:18:21.180
Let's see, Mr. Juan Carlos Barbieri.

00:18:21.180 --> 00:18:26.620
Did the scenes with Norma Jiménez in "El Tambor de Sacuarí" turn out easy?

00:18:26.620 --> 00:18:28.820
To kiss such a pretty girl is very simple.

00:18:28.820 --> 00:18:30.000
And the question you asked.

00:18:30.410 --> 00:18:32.750
- I suggest Borcosque do it. - Nice to meet you.

00:18:33.000 --> 00:18:35.380
- Tulio, get closer. - Are you going to rush it?

00:18:35.460 --> 00:18:38.580
- I'm going. - When will Tulio start directing?

00:18:38.660 --> 00:18:41.550
- In a few days. - Then you'll see what happens.

00:18:41.630 --> 00:18:45.520
And so ends a new edition of Radio Belgrano's Cinema Diary,

00:18:45.540 --> 00:18:49.040
which had the collaboration of Gloria Grey, Domingo Di Nubila...

00:18:49.120 --> 00:18:51.800
- Carlos Borcosque, Juan Carlos Barbieri... - And Tulio De Vicheli.

00:18:51.880 --> 00:18:53.880
Directed by Chas de Cruz.

00:18:59.250 --> 00:19:00.000
We're going to...

00:19:00.000 --> 00:19:01.880
Let's try a little Provincialist, huh?

00:19:01.880 --> 00:19:06.550
Thank you very much.

00:19:06.550 --> 00:19:07.550
And how's that spirit going?

00:19:07.550 --> 00:19:08.550
Oh, I'm dead.

00:19:08.550 --> 00:19:09.550
Don't be afraid.

00:19:09.550 --> 00:19:11.910
When I recommend someone, I know why I do it.

00:19:11.910 --> 00:19:12.910
Silence, please.

00:19:12.910 --> 00:19:13.800
Good luck.

00:19:13.800 --> 00:19:16.000
Thank you.

00:19:16.000 --> 00:19:20.520
Now, a native music audition in charge of the "Los Pampeanos" ensemble.

00:19:20.520 --> 00:19:25.610
In the first term, a song "Sun and Moon" by an anonymous author, with intervention

00:19:25.610 --> 00:19:26.650
from Lidia Jiménez.

00:19:48.790 --> 00:19:51.830
What are you looking at?

00:20:01.210 --> 00:20:07.570
Love, even if I'm on my way, I have to wait.

00:20:08.490 --> 00:20:16.360
I like the moon, I like the sun that took it away from me.

00:21:10.110 --> 00:21:12.910
- Very good, Lidia, very good. - Magnificent. What do you think, Gloria?

00:21:12.910 --> 00:21:14.340
- Very good. - Splendid.

00:21:14.340 --> 00:21:17.090
We'll hire her.

00:21:30.090 --> 00:21:32.560
when you learn not to run and to speak correctly.

00:21:32.600 --> 00:21:34.580
What's that about a half-court goal?

00:21:34.650 --> 00:21:37.650
It's said that Mrs. Lidia had a great success.

00:21:37.660 --> 00:21:39.510
- Oh, my God! - Yes, Mrs. Lidia.

00:21:42.860 --> 00:21:45.580
Excuse me?

00:21:46.610 --> 00:21:49.590
Mrs. Lidia had a great success.

00:21:49.780 --> 00:21:52.980
And you say it like that. It's something more than a great success.

00:21:53.090 --> 00:21:55.000
She scored a half-court goal.

00:21:55.160 --> 00:21:59.640
- You're right. - Like no one else.

00:22:00.540 --> 00:22:04.860
"I was carrying the child of the

00:22:04.860 --> 00:22:07.980
"It seems that the reunion is complete."

00:22:07.980 --> 00:22:10.140
"More or less. Do you like how it looks beautiful?"

00:22:10.140 --> 00:22:13.310
"It's beautiful. It reminds me of Lípide, boy."

00:22:13.310 --> 00:22:15.050
"For rent, it's not bad."

00:22:15.050 --> 00:22:17.010
"You'll see that I buy later tonight."

00:22:17.010 --> 00:22:18.060
"I touched wood."

00:22:18.060 --> 00:22:20.030
"What? Are you in a chair?"

00:22:20.030 --> 00:22:22.410
"Take this to the kitchen."

00:22:22.410 --> 00:22:24.500
"How did it go?"

00:22:24.500 --> 00:22:25.600
"Thank God, very well."

00:22:25.600 --> 00:22:27.390
"We were waiting for you to congratulate her."

00:22:27.390 --> 00:22:30.000
"We didn't hear you, but we know that you sang divinely."

00:22:30.000 --> 00:22:32.400
Miss Lydia, what luck! I congratulate you!

00:22:32.400 --> 00:22:35.100
Now that luck has begun, be careful, girl.

00:22:35.100 --> 00:22:37.460
It's a pity that you have to spend yourself singing on the radio.

00:22:37.460 --> 00:22:38.960
It seems little to you?

00:22:38.960 --> 00:22:41.680
If it were the cinema or the theater, but the radio.

00:22:41.680 --> 00:22:43.680
I wish I could get a contract.

00:22:43.680 --> 00:22:45.180
The tour is coming.

00:22:45.180 --> 00:22:47.170
Did you get so elegant to welcome me?

00:22:47.170 --> 00:22:49.670
No, I'm also going to look for the triumph.

00:22:49.670 --> 00:22:50.670
This is my night.

00:22:50.670 --> 00:22:52.980
At last I will be able to prove what I am capable of.

00:22:52.980 --> 00:22:54.530
Oh, then good luck!

00:22:54.530 --> 00:22:56.830
That one? I have it with me.

00:22:57.830 --> 00:22:59.890
Come with me.

00:23:06.140 --> 00:23:13.540
"Alone, always alone, since you left."

00:23:14.820 --> 00:23:21.520
"Alone, with my sorrow, is that I am so sad."

00:23:21.520 --> 00:23:25.350
"A street without a course."

00:23:40.260 --> 00:23:43.280
Why did you come to Smokey?

00:23:44.280 --> 00:23:46.280
I thought it was what corresponded.

00:23:47.260 --> 00:23:48.620
In any case, I'm leaving.

00:23:49.620 --> 00:23:51.620
No, since you are staying.

00:23:53.650 --> 00:23:57.000
The one who is playing is Blanca.

00:23:58.010 --> 00:24:00.000
Ah, Blanca.

00:24:01.980 --> 00:24:19.460
Maria Ofelia, who's that guy who came from Smoky?

00:24:19.460 --> 00:24:23.050
Poor boy, he looks like a young man from the countryside.

00:24:23.050 --> 00:24:25.050
Now we're talking.

00:24:25.050 --> 00:24:29.380
I'll serve you a whiskey, please.

00:24:30.640 --> 00:24:33.840
- No, I'm not that kind of person. - Ah, see?

00:24:36.170 --> 00:24:42.260
It's unworthy to make fun of a poor boy like that.

00:24:43.320 --> 00:24:45.160
What are you doing here, all alone?

00:24:45.820 --> 00:24:47.960
You see? You're the one with the cross, right?

00:24:48.090 --> 00:24:51.220
And you, Mariano Martínez? I know you from the radio.

00:24:51.810 --> 00:24:53.910
I'm trying to open my path as a composer.

00:24:54.110 --> 00:24:57.200
Good. You're going to make it, friend. You have the conditions.

00:24:57.530 --> 00:24:58.550
Very kind.

00:25:00.670 --> 00:25:03.070
- In a song... - Hello, Charlie.

00:25:03.170 --> 00:25:05.590
- Hello, Del Monte. - Come in.

00:25:05.690 --> 00:25:08.590
Here we are with this young lady, who is a true promise.

00:25:08.690 --> 00:25:11.010
- Miss Ruby. - Hello, Miss.

00:25:11.090 --> 00:25:13.100
- Did you notice the blonde in Del Monte? - Who is she?

00:25:13.200 --> 00:25:15.600
- That guy is a fiend. - How can he be so beautiful?

00:25:15.700 --> 00:25:17.500
With the story of the movie "Cine Finestriato"...

00:25:17.600 --> 00:25:19.440
...he deceives so many pure girls.

00:25:20.120 --> 00:25:22.620
Tell me, how did you do...

00:25:22.720 --> 00:25:28.940
...to drown...

00:25:29.040 --> 00:25:30.000
...that I alone...

00:25:30.860 --> 00:25:35.830
I wonder, anguished, how to live

00:26:01.660 --> 00:26:05.600
- Who invited you? - A great pianist.

00:26:06.010 --> 00:26:07.880
- Do you want me to introduce him? - Later.

00:26:09.210 --> 00:26:12.220
I'll ask him to play. He's a good composer.

00:26:14.000 --> 00:26:16.590
- That's the moment. Play now. - What do you think?

00:26:16.790 --> 00:26:19.090
- I told Ponce de León. - There's too much noise.

00:26:19.290 --> 00:26:21.590
- Start. I'll take care of the piano. - Okay.

00:26:22.970 --> 00:26:26.080
You have an invitee. Now you have to put up with that guy's music.

00:26:26.440 --> 00:26:28.040
What do you want me to do? It's not easy.

00:26:28.250 --> 00:26:30.000
- I'll give it to you. - Guys!

00:26:30.440 --> 00:26:46.090
- I invite you to come to something. - Madre mía!

00:26:46.090 --> 00:26:48.100
He's a bad guy. I fell asleep waiting for him.

00:26:48.100 --> 00:26:59.410
Nobody is more elegant than you, Luciano, right?

00:27:03.390 --> 00:27:06.460
- It must've been a goal from half-court. - It was a great goal.

00:27:06.460 --> 00:27:09.800
How lucky. I wish I'd liked to go.

00:27:09.800 --> 00:27:12.900
Come on, tell me. Tell me everything.

00:27:12.900 --> 00:27:17.360
- I've never been to a party. - There were a lot of people.

00:27:17.360 --> 00:27:23.040
I can imagine. The lights, the lady's dresses, the jewels.

00:27:23.040 --> 00:27:25.540
At first, you were a bit shy.

00:27:25.540 --> 00:27:29.860
Then, when they asked you to play the piano, who asked you to play?

00:27:31.120 --> 00:27:34.710
- I don't know. I don't remember. - What did he do to you?

00:27:34.830 --> 00:27:39.640
I'm a boy who has a song and needs someone to hear it.

00:27:39.960 --> 00:27:44.850
- And he did a great job. - With an honor of silence.

00:27:45.650 --> 00:27:47.890
I remembered your handkerchief.

00:27:48.590 --> 00:27:51.410
I thought of all the tears he cries.

00:27:52.230 --> 00:27:57.520
So as not to break that emotion, I started to smile.

00:28:04.000 --> 00:28:04.480
Thank you.

00:28:33.640 --> 00:28:41.550
but that white star will always, always come out.

00:28:41.550 --> 00:28:44.770
Through bitter paths, failure returns,

00:28:44.770 --> 00:28:51.470
and through those paths, you become a dream.

00:28:51.470 --> 00:28:54.870
Suddenly, your own step resonates,

00:28:54.870 --> 00:29:00.000
as if it were the echo of some memory.

00:29:20.090 --> 00:29:22.020
-

00:29:30.030 --> 00:29:38.040
I'm going to say goodbye.

00:30:13.950 --> 00:30:18.100
I would have given you anything you asked for.

00:30:18.300 --> 00:30:23.040
Diego, I thank you with all my heart for waiting for me.

00:30:35.690 --> 00:30:37.190
Pay me at least two monthly.

00:30:37.190 --> 00:30:39.290
And why don't you take that condemned Piano at once?

00:30:39.290 --> 00:30:40.490
If I take him, I won't fix anything.

00:30:40.490 --> 00:30:41.690
What I want is for him to pay me.

00:30:41.690 --> 00:30:44.370
We don't have money. Take him and that's it.

00:30:44.370 --> 00:30:46.650
Mrs. María Blanca, Mr. Mariano needs him.

00:30:46.650 --> 00:30:49.050
Mr. Mariano needs food, not Piano.

00:30:49.050 --> 00:30:51.250
That Piano is like a friend to Mr. Mariano.

00:30:51.250 --> 00:30:54.130
If you need a friend, get yourself a dog, cheaper.

00:30:54.130 --> 00:30:56.240
You know it. Take him whenever you want.

00:30:56.240 --> 00:30:59.120
What a joke.

00:31:00.030 --> 00:31:02.030
No, two at least. They owe me six.

00:31:02.030 --> 00:31:03.860
Maybe Mr. Mariano will pay you one.

00:31:03.860 --> 00:31:05.860
And next month, the ladies will start the day.

00:31:05.860 --> 00:31:06.860
I don't like it.

00:31:06.860 --> 00:31:08.820
Don't be like that. You need the piano.

00:31:08.820 --> 00:31:10.770
Okay, but they'll pay me right now, okay?

00:31:10.770 --> 00:31:11.770
I won't return anything another day.

00:31:11.770 --> 00:31:13.770
Yes, yes, yes, just a moment. I'm going to tell Mr. Mariano.

00:31:13.770 --> 00:31:14.770
It's me or it's not me?

00:31:14.770 --> 00:31:25.020
I'm grateful to you in my soul, but I can't accept it.

00:31:25.020 --> 00:31:28.860
If I needed money, wouldn't you lend it to me?

00:31:30.000 --> 00:31:35.080
- That doesn't mean you have to lend it to me. - Please don't, I don't want it.

00:31:35.830 --> 00:31:37.790
Don't worry, I'll sort it out.

00:31:38.020 --> 00:31:41.110
If things get very bad, I can ask my uncle Alejandro for help.

00:31:41.490 --> 00:31:42.960
Thank you, Andrés.

00:32:03.040 --> 00:32:07.790
- Here it is. - Fine.

00:32:07.790 --> 00:32:09.830
But at the end of the month, without fail, it's delayed.

00:32:09.830 --> 00:32:11.330
Don't worry, I'll answer.

00:32:35.400 --> 00:32:37.200
- Here's Mr. Martínez. - From whom?

00:32:37.240 --> 00:32:40.890
- From his uncle Alejandro. - Mr. Martínez, your uncle is looking for you.

00:32:41.100 --> 00:32:51.620
- Coming! - Is all the clothes there?

00:32:51.870 --> 00:32:54.370
- Now finish the stairs. - I already did it, miss.

00:32:54.410 --> 00:32:56.580
Yes, very dirty, you left the last steps.

00:32:56.600 --> 00:32:58.710
Grab that bucket and go to pass them a cloth again.

00:33:06.010 --> 00:33:07.890
That's my life, and I can't give up.

00:33:07.890 --> 00:33:09.280
But you have a future there.

00:33:09.280 --> 00:33:12.870
If I leave the hardware store it's because I'm tired and not because the business isn't good.

00:33:12.870 --> 00:33:14.500
You pay me as much as you can.

00:33:14.500 --> 00:33:16.680
- I don't care. - Think about it.

00:33:16.680 --> 00:33:19.520
It's an injustice that I have to leave you in a strange place.

00:33:19.520 --> 00:33:22.360
Why are you going around if you can have a safe life?

00:33:22.360 --> 00:33:25.120
Don't insist, uncle. I chose a path.

00:33:25.120 --> 00:33:28.200
My music, my tangos, and I can't go back.

00:33:28.200 --> 00:33:29.730
How are you going to regret it?

00:33:31.020 --> 00:33:39.600
- Bye, Mayra. - I like it that way.

00:33:39.600 --> 00:33:43.640
It's very ugly to listen to conversations.

00:33:43.640 --> 00:33:46.360
Keep cleaning the floor, that's what you're here for.

00:33:46.360 --> 00:33:54.320
Daniel didn't bring me the shirt.

00:33:54.320 --> 00:33:57.490
- Would you wash this one? - Yes, Mr. Ramos.

00:33:57.490 --> 00:34:00.000
- That's why I'm here. - You're going to have to...

00:34:00.000 --> 00:34:02.050
Don't worry, it will be like new.

00:34:02.150 --> 00:34:05.370
Well, I'll pay you tomorrow, because now I'm without change.

00:34:05.470 --> 00:34:07.520
It doesn't matter, you have credit with me.

00:34:07.620 --> 00:34:10.470
Ah, but it's not more than 60 cents anymore, and now it's a peso.

00:34:10.570 --> 00:34:12.470
A peso? That's crazy.

00:34:12.570 --> 00:34:14.870
Life is going up.

00:34:14.970 --> 00:34:16.480
Don't worry, I'll pay you tomorrow.

00:34:31.120 --> 00:34:35.380
Don't laugh at me. I had to charge him more because someone has to pay for the piano.

00:34:35.850 --> 00:34:40.500
Silvia, why do I have to pay for the piano when he treats me so badly?

00:34:40.620 --> 00:34:46.130
We have to forgive him. Things are not going well for him. He's a great musician.

00:34:47.170 --> 00:34:57.970
- Good morning, sir. - Hello, Marianito.

00:34:58.050 --> 00:34:59.760
- I have something new for you. - Oh, yes?

00:35:00.000 --> 00:35:02.350
Maybe he's interested in Di Pietro. Do you know him?

00:35:02.450 --> 00:35:05.350
- Who doesn't know Di Pietro's orchestra? - It's a bolero.

00:35:05.450 --> 00:35:08.120
- No, it's a tango. - A tango.

00:35:08.220 --> 00:35:11.890
- What do you think? - Play it, so I can't notice.

00:35:11.990 --> 00:35:14.570
- But you don't compose? - Of course I compose.

00:35:14.670 --> 00:35:16.590
- But I play it. - How?

00:35:16.690 --> 00:35:20.410
And yes, I play music to a friend of mine, and he writes it for me.

00:35:20.510 --> 00:35:28.610
- Ah. - Let's go, maestro.

00:36:05.720 --> 00:36:08.950
- You're Enrique Delfino, right? - Yes.

00:36:09.150 --> 00:36:11.610
I appreciate your opinion. I know what you're worth.

00:36:11.810 --> 00:36:13.930
But your music is missing something.

00:36:14.130 --> 00:36:16.050
It's inspired, but not popular.

00:36:16.250 --> 00:36:18.460
- Why? - For a music to be popular...

00:36:18.660 --> 00:36:20.660
...we all have to recognize in it something of ours.

00:36:20.860 --> 00:36:22.860
The pain, the joy, the hope.

00:36:23.060 --> 00:36:26.260
A music triumphs not when it's played by a great orchestra...

00:36:26.460 --> 00:36:30.000
...but when it's played by a little organ.

00:36:30.030 --> 00:36:32.030
I don't know how to get that.

00:36:32.030 --> 00:36:36.160
Suffering, suffering and seeing others suffer.

00:36:36.160 --> 00:36:39.760
Work, boy, and get as close as you can to life.

00:36:39.760 --> 00:36:42.060
She will teach you.

00:36:42.060 --> 00:36:52.180
- What do you think? - The melody is beautiful.

00:36:52.180 --> 00:36:54.930
- If you want, I'll give you 100 pesos. - What did he say?

00:36:54.930 --> 00:36:56.760
In the end, we could get to 150.

00:36:56.760 --> 00:37:00.000
We have to work on this tango.

00:37:00.190 --> 00:37:03.190
- But do you want to work with me? - Work, you say?

00:37:03.190 --> 00:37:07.550
- No, old man, I'll sign it. - No, don't sign it.

00:37:07.550 --> 00:37:11.720
Here's something of my life and I haven't settled enough to sell it.

00:37:11.720 --> 00:37:16.820
- Very good. - I would have done the same.

00:37:16.820 --> 00:37:22.220
- Don't ever sell yourself, old man. - You don't know how much I needed those 100 pesos.

00:37:22.220 --> 00:37:24.460
- How are you, Lidia? How are you? - Better.

00:37:24.460 --> 00:37:28.450
- Better or not? - This afternoon he went to the radio and came to misery.

00:37:30.030 --> 00:37:34.140
- What are you going to film? - It's a real opportunity.

00:37:34.140 --> 00:37:37.040
There's each one. Look what to film at night.

00:37:37.040 --> 00:37:40.100
I came to tell the director about a record.

00:37:40.100 --> 00:37:42.920
I didn't expect it to be true.

00:37:42.920 --> 00:37:44.380
It's already finished.

00:37:44.380 --> 00:37:49.120
- Give it to me. - Will you come with me?

00:37:49.120 --> 00:37:53.410
Poor Mrs. Amanda.

00:37:53.410 --> 00:37:55.440
- The director... - It's starting to go well.

00:37:55.440 --> 00:37:58.550
Of all of us, I'm the only one who doesn't talk to her.

00:37:58.550 --> 00:37:59.760
Don't say anything.

00:38:00.280 --> 00:38:03.880
- You have to keep working. - I don't know if it's worth it.

00:38:04.370 --> 00:38:08.710
Do you want me to tell you the truth? What they told you is true.

00:38:09.620 --> 00:38:13.940
It's not enough that the music is good. It must reach everyone's heart.

00:38:15.170 --> 00:38:21.420
So that a song triumphs, it has to make a nest in the soul of humble people.

00:38:23.400 --> 00:38:29.760
You may be right. With everything, let's see what happens tonight.

00:38:30.000 --> 00:38:32.120
- Where are you going? - To Llegalón.

00:38:33.330 --> 00:38:35.830
Lucia asked Delmonte to introduce me to this.

00:38:40.870 --> 00:38:45.680
I can't wait for Delmonte. I want to move out.

00:38:46.030 --> 00:38:49.500
Son, when you're asked for favors, you have to know how to handle it.

00:38:49.700 --> 00:38:53.200
- You have to deal with every guy. - Don't be like that.

00:38:53.400 --> 00:38:56.200
- I should go look for the girl he has now. - The one from the other day?

00:38:56.400 --> 00:39:00.000
- No. He changes women all the time. - I don't know what to do with him.

00:39:00.640 --> 00:39:01.350
What do you see in it?

00:39:01.690 --> 00:39:04.070
To walk well dressed, to wear real shoes,

00:39:04.110 --> 00:39:06.660
to have a nice apartment, to drive around in a car.

00:39:06.760 --> 00:39:08.450
And does that seem like a lot?

00:39:08.490 --> 00:39:10.820
I don't know, but it's so difficult,

00:39:10.950 --> 00:39:12.520
so horrible to fight with life,

00:39:12.920 --> 00:39:14.920
to reject temptations all the time.

00:39:15.810 --> 00:39:17.360
It's better not to think.

00:39:18.060 --> 00:39:20.410
Look, there's Del Monte.

00:39:32.490 --> 00:39:34.510
- How are you, Martínez? - How are you?

00:39:34.920 --> 00:39:38.930
- Do you know the young lady? - No, I just met her.

00:40:00.730 --> 00:40:03.390
- I'll fix it. - I'm going to look for her.

00:40:09.320 --> 00:40:12.920
- How are things going? - Fine.

00:40:13.090 --> 00:40:15.190
What do you think of the girl I introduced you to?

00:40:15.300 --> 00:40:17.590
Poor girl.

00:40:18.310 --> 00:40:22.370
The arena is over. Let's go.

00:40:22.420 --> 00:40:24.680
- I'll introduce you to her. - No, I'm not interested.

00:40:30.320 --> 00:40:32.920
Sonsa, you still believe in words.

00:40:33.270 --> 00:40:35.710
- Do you want some advice? - I went with Delmonte.

00:40:36.010 --> 00:40:39.510
But don't listen to Mariano.

00:40:39.730 --> 00:40:41.720
He still gets his way.

00:40:41.860 --> 00:40:45.890
- I don't know. - Go with Delmonte until you find someone better.

00:40:46.190 --> 00:40:49.400
There's no need to lose any opportunity in life.

00:40:50.000 --> 00:40:52.060
And you, then? Why did you go with Mariano?

00:40:52.380 --> 00:40:56.040
Because I like him. But that's a part of my life.

00:40:56.610 --> 00:40:59.000
The other has nothing to do with feelings.

00:41:00.030 --> 00:41:08.680
I assure you. Come on, let's go.

00:41:08.680 --> 00:41:11.560
Wait for me outside for a moment. I forgot the letter.

00:41:56.170 --> 00:41:58.960
- Who was that guy? - And you?

00:42:03.070 --> 00:42:04.680
And no one came out here.

00:42:09.860 --> 00:42:12.550
I thought it was someone who was at your friend's party.

00:42:12.890 --> 00:42:15.590
- A painter. - I don't know.

00:42:16.530 --> 00:42:20.020
- I was alone all day. - You say so.

00:42:22.720 --> 00:42:28.090
- Do you think I'm cheating on you? - With you you can never be very sure.

00:42:31.210 --> 00:42:35.540
- Mariano, I know what's wrong with you. - What's wrong with me?

00:42:36.970 --> 00:42:41.900
That you're in trouble. You have no money and you don't know how to make a living.

00:42:42.000 --> 00:42:42.970
I'll make a living.

00:42:43.860 --> 00:42:48.420
Writing tango. Come on, get it out of your head.

00:42:51.130 --> 00:42:55.160
But, if you'd listen to me, I could help you.

00:42:55.250 --> 00:42:58.870
- How? - I know a man who owns a confectionery chain.

00:43:00.440 --> 00:43:03.960
If you want, we'll go see him and he proposes to form a great orchestra.

00:43:04.160 --> 00:43:06.080
I don't have enough prestige for that.

00:43:06.190 --> 00:43:08.380
It doesn't matter.

00:43:09.240 --> 00:43:14.130
We'll get ahead of him and then I'll take care of it.

00:43:15.260 --> 00:43:16.790
The guy is married, you know?

00:43:17.520 --> 00:43:19.570
And no one likes domestic deals.

00:43:19.860 --> 00:43:22.540
We haven't fallen so low as to do those things.

00:43:22.930 --> 00:43:25.960
Look, Mariano, I've been meaning to tell you this for a long time.

00:43:27.030 --> 00:43:28.580
I grab myself with the nails I can.

00:43:30.000 --> 00:43:32.160
I only saw him once. Do you hear me?

00:43:32.160 --> 00:43:34.110
No, don't look at me with disgust.

00:43:34.110 --> 00:43:36.790
You and I are a couple of unhappy,

00:43:36.790 --> 00:43:37.790
heavy, despised.

00:43:37.790 --> 00:43:39.710
Why so much pride?

00:43:39.710 --> 00:43:41.630
So much dignity of a starving man?

00:43:41.630 --> 00:43:43.520
You have to learn the truth.

00:43:43.520 --> 00:43:45.520
Because if you don't, you'll continue to be a coward,

00:43:45.520 --> 00:43:47.190
a failure.

00:43:47.190 --> 00:43:50.430
If for you the truth is to have to roll over in the mud,

00:43:50.430 --> 00:43:54.220
I prefer to continue to be a coward, a failure.

00:43:54.220 --> 00:43:59.960
You're not going to have to put up with me anymore.

00:44:12.890 --> 00:44:16.320
Miss Lidia is very ill, the doctor came. I'm going to the pharmacy to get this remedy.

00:44:36.750 --> 00:44:39.510
- Mariana. - You're better, aren't you?

00:44:40.240 --> 00:44:43.090
- I don't want to die here. - How?

00:44:43.540 --> 00:44:45.680
Now people die for a nun.

00:44:45.820 --> 00:44:47.580
I want to go back to my land.

00:44:48.120 --> 00:44:52.440
First you get better, and then you go on a month's assault.

00:44:52.650 --> 00:44:55.350
An assault for a month? That's not a bad idea.

00:44:55.710 --> 00:44:58.310
Well, now leave me alone with the young lady.

00:44:58.520 --> 00:45:00.000
I have to apply an injection.

00:45:06.460 --> 00:45:09.990
- We'll have to send him to the hospital. - To the hospital?

00:45:09.990 --> 00:45:12.050
- But, ma'am... - I'm going crazy, ma'am.

00:45:12.050 --> 00:45:15.140
What do you want me to do? Who's going to pay for all this?

00:45:15.140 --> 00:45:19.650
The doctor, the medicines... Who has money in this house?

00:45:19.650 --> 00:45:22.670
Don't worry, I'm going to get it. I'm going to pay for it all.

00:45:22.670 --> 00:45:25.320
- What would you call him? - On this sunset.

00:45:25.320 --> 00:45:27.280
- A nice guy. - He likes it.

00:45:27.280 --> 00:45:29.960
- Of course, a lot. - What else, if he has two hundred pesos.

00:45:32.040 --> 00:45:40.400
- Can't you give me something else? - Thank you.

00:45:43.020 --> 00:45:45.680
Tell me, will there be any service in your orchestra?

00:45:45.880 --> 00:45:47.860
I'm sorry, but I have to go to camp.

00:45:49.060 --> 00:45:50.600
- And as a copyist? - Neither.

00:45:51.190 --> 00:45:53.360
But if you're in need, I can get you something.

00:45:53.420 --> 00:45:56.050
- Where? - The place, you know, is not...

00:45:56.360 --> 00:45:57.860
It's not very recommended.

00:46:30.030 --> 00:46:37.880
If you asked me to go out with him, I wouldn't say no.

00:46:37.880 --> 00:46:40.700
You're crazy! If he hears you, he'll kill you.

00:47:08.220 --> 00:47:10.420
- What time is it? - 2:30 p.m.

00:47:10.890 --> 00:47:12.740
Time goes by so fast.

00:47:13.020 --> 00:47:15.200
It's like that in the beginning, you'll get used to it later.

00:47:16.500 --> 00:47:19.840
I'll be here a little longer, until I get something else.

00:47:20.240 --> 00:47:23.270
Don't worry, son. I told you, it's been ten years.

00:47:24.520 --> 00:47:26.500
Life goes round and round.

00:47:28.070 --> 00:47:30.000
When I was a boy, I dreamed of a coffee shop.

00:47:30.000 --> 00:47:35.430
Someone like him wrote a tango.

00:47:36.560 --> 00:47:37.360
Music.

00:47:55.600 --> 00:47:58.900
These things that are never enough...

00:48:00.000 --> 00:48:09.860
against the life that was only later living just like mine.

00:48:09.860 --> 00:48:18.240
In the school of all things, Chacho, you gave me in amazement

00:48:18.240 --> 00:48:27.270
the cigarette, the pen and the dream of a hope of love.

00:49:00.000 --> 00:49:05.330
A cruel day of not thinking of me anymore

00:49:09.800 --> 00:49:12.310
Not a single bit of me

00:49:13.430 --> 00:49:18.300
That are the same things that encourage me to cry

00:49:18.670 --> 00:49:20.470
José de la Quimera

00:49:20.670 --> 00:49:24.730
Marcial who still believes in her

00:49:24.930 --> 00:49:27.730
And the flaco Abel who left us

00:49:27.930 --> 00:49:30.000
But still guides me

00:49:33.070 --> 00:49:35.900
the ones that never ask.

00:49:37.150 --> 00:49:39.650
One afternoon, the first deception

00:49:40.330 --> 00:49:44.850
was born in the sorrows of years.

00:49:49.090 --> 00:49:56.630
I asked...

00:50:01.240 --> 00:50:09.370
the only thing in life that resembled my old age.

00:50:09.370 --> 00:50:22.200
Your miracle-looking mixture made me learn philosophy,

00:50:22.200 --> 00:50:30.000
the cruel poetry of not thinking about me anymore.

00:50:40.720 --> 00:50:42.280
There are sick people in the house.

00:50:42.280 --> 00:50:44.060
I'll scream as much as I want, that's what you owe me.

00:50:44.060 --> 00:50:45.560
You're going to pay, I promise.

00:50:45.560 --> 00:50:48.400
Tomorrow I come with the truck, and they pay me or I take the piano.

00:51:03.900 --> 00:51:06.840
- How is Mr. Martínez? - He hasn't come yet.

00:51:07.260 --> 00:51:09.920
- You're Mrs. Lucía, right? - Yes.

00:51:10.170 --> 00:51:12.420
- And you're Clarita, right? - Yes.

00:51:12.520 --> 00:51:14.460
Margarita has talked a lot about you.

00:51:14.630 --> 00:51:16.970
- You don't know when you'll be back. - Later.

00:51:17.170 --> 00:51:20.010
- And how are you? - Very busy.

00:51:20.130 --> 00:51:23.370
- I have to do my job. - Tell him to come see you.

00:51:23.490 --> 00:51:26.350
- He'll be happy. - Haven't you seen each other for a while?

00:51:26.470 --> 00:51:30.000
We had a little disagreement, but we'll sort it out.

00:51:31.180 --> 00:51:35.220
- I know he loves me very much. He can't live without me. - Yes, of course.

00:51:35.540 --> 00:51:39.090
- Besides, the lack of money is bad for him. - It's true.

00:51:39.090 --> 00:51:42.690
- And now that he's going to stay without me, it'll be worse. - Why would he stay without you?

00:51:42.790 --> 00:51:46.740
He owes me a certain amount of money. I paid what I could, but I can't take it anymore.

00:51:47.040 --> 00:51:50.870
- Couldn't you help me? - Is that what you owe me?

00:51:51.040 --> 00:51:53.970
No. If we had the money, we could keep going.

00:51:54.090 --> 00:52:00.000
- If you dare to do anything, I'm ashamed. - I'm not ashamed at all. - Then?

00:52:05.440 --> 00:52:09.460
You take this ring, you keep the $50 from the piano and you give me the rest.

00:52:10.570 --> 00:52:13.020
Oh, don't tell Mariano anything.

00:52:13.230 --> 00:52:30.000
- Be careful. - Okay.

00:52:30.480 --> 00:52:33.800
- Yes, quite a lot. - I'll give you 300 pesos.

00:52:33.800 --> 00:52:41.090
- Okay. - Where did you get this ring?

00:52:41.090 --> 00:52:44.500
- It's not mine, it's a friend's. - Oh, and where do you live?

00:52:44.500 --> 00:52:47.050
Here, in the Orillana pension, in Paraná y Corrientes.

00:52:47.050 --> 00:52:51.560
- Okay, take it. - Thank you very much, ma'am.

00:52:51.560 --> 00:52:57.710
- Miss Roca Esther, what's wrong with you? - Lidia is like this, in the hall, with everyone.

00:52:57.710 --> 00:52:59.830
- Why did they take her down? - She asked for it.

00:53:00.000 --> 00:53:02.790
And the doctor says that there's no reason to deny anything.

00:53:12.330 --> 00:53:13.600
It's all so beautiful.

00:53:14.590 --> 00:53:17.030
Look, we say that the house is for the poor.

00:53:18.230 --> 00:53:21.150
The poor is a little ruined, but it's not for so many.

00:53:22.010 --> 00:53:24.700
On the other hand, when I arrived, it seemed like a palace to me.

00:53:24.890 --> 00:53:28.770
A palace in the front and a convent in the back.

00:53:28.920 --> 00:53:30.000
When people...

00:53:31.240 --> 00:53:34.820
- I don't care about the house. - I don't feel so comfortable.

00:53:34.900 --> 00:53:42.310
- I was afraid yesterday in my room. - You're happy, aren't you?

00:53:42.390 --> 00:53:48.600
I'm happy. They asked for a favor. I would do it.

00:53:48.680 --> 00:53:52.030
- Tell me about it. - Talk about it.

00:53:52.110 --> 00:54:00.000
Now they're coming to talk to me a few times.

00:54:00.120 --> 00:54:05.700
- We're all together. - That's why we're all together.

00:54:05.700 --> 00:54:09.700
Sometimes people don't see each other for a long time.

00:54:09.700 --> 00:54:15.970
- When someone leaves, we always meet again. - In life.

00:54:15.970 --> 00:54:25.340
- In life. - Don't make me insist.

00:54:25.340 --> 00:54:29.380
- You know I can't talk to you. - Naturally, Mariano.

00:54:32.460 --> 00:54:39.890
- What do you want me to sing? - My song of antipathy.

00:56:40.910 --> 00:56:43.560
In peace. He's happier than all of us.

00:56:43.560 --> 00:56:46.030
It's very easy to be happier than any of us.

00:56:46.030 --> 00:56:49.750
- Life can also be good. - Life is good for those who have money.

00:56:49.750 --> 00:56:52.270
No, life is not good.

00:56:52.270 --> 00:56:54.570
I only knew insinuations and tears.

00:56:54.570 --> 00:56:56.430
Life never gave me anything.

00:56:56.430 --> 00:57:00.000
It can be good for those who have everything, but not for us, those who drag ourselves

00:57:33.770 --> 00:57:37.080
- She's leaving, Amanda. - I can't stand this life.

00:57:37.180 --> 00:57:40.740
You're crazy, girl. You don't know the life you're going to live.

00:57:40.790 --> 00:57:44.980
I wasn't born to be poor. It costs everything to have what you want.

00:57:45.080 --> 00:57:48.520
- And Gerardo? - I found your wife.

00:57:48.560 --> 00:57:51.120
- He's leaving without saying anything. - I'll let you talk to him.

00:58:06.080 --> 00:58:10.770
- Why do you let us, Gerardo? - I got a job at the Formosa factory.

00:58:10.770 --> 00:58:16.220
- We're going very far. - The further away from this city, the better.

00:58:16.220 --> 00:58:20.100
- What if one day Amanda comes back? - She won't come back.

00:58:20.100 --> 00:58:23.150
- You don't know her. - Miss Sorillana?

00:58:23.150 --> 00:58:26.380
- It's us. What did you want? - I'm Inspector Menendez.

00:58:26.380 --> 00:58:28.480
- And the police? - Investigations.

00:58:28.480 --> 00:58:30.000
You must be mistaken, Inspector.

00:58:30.410 --> 00:58:33.890
- This is a house of respectful people. - It's about the robbery of a ring.

00:58:34.250 --> 00:58:36.130
- I don't know anything else. - Ah, you don't know anything else, huh?

00:58:36.130 --> 00:58:38.040
- No, sir, nothing else. - Let's see if you remember.

00:58:38.040 --> 00:58:40.150
- The one who gave you the ring, what's his name? - No one gave it to me.

00:58:40.150 --> 00:58:42.930
- Was it a man or a woman? - I think I found it on the street.

00:58:42.930 --> 00:58:44.370
- On what street? - I don't remember.

00:58:44.370 --> 00:58:47.520
- I saw you giving the money to a guy when you left El Espeño. - I didn't give him anything.

00:58:47.520 --> 00:58:50.670
- Where's the rest? - I spent it. I don't remember.

00:58:50.670 --> 00:58:52.970
- Since when do you know that guy? - Who?

00:58:52.970 --> 00:58:56.930
- The one who gave you the ring! - No one gave it to me!

00:58:56.930 --> 00:58:59.570
You must have found it on the street, as they say.

00:59:00.320 --> 00:59:02.240
I'm convinced he left it in the water.

00:59:02.770 --> 00:59:04.380
I remember it perfectly.

00:59:04.590 --> 00:59:07.920
I was washing my hands, and there were two young ladies.

00:59:08.210 --> 00:59:11.530
One of them, blonde, with a black dress.

00:59:11.730 --> 00:59:15.700
You're lying. I know you well, and I know you're capable of anything.

00:59:15.900 --> 00:59:17.870
I have nothing to do with that matter.

00:59:18.070 --> 00:59:19.570
Get out of here and leave me alone.

00:59:19.770 --> 00:59:21.290
You gave the ring to the girl.

00:59:21.490 --> 00:59:22.760
That slut is a thief.

00:59:22.950 --> 00:59:25.960
I swear you'll tell me the truth or I'll report you.

00:59:26.270 --> 00:59:28.380
Fine. I found the ring that night.

00:59:31.920 --> 00:59:35.480
- Here's the money, give it back. - You're going to take it to the police yourself.

00:59:35.510 --> 00:59:39.730
You're crazy. Now that I think about it, I'm an idiot to tell you that.

00:59:39.930 --> 00:59:42.550
Because that little girl wouldn't tell me anything.

00:59:43.490 --> 00:59:46.030
She'd hold on to anything in order not to give herself away.

00:59:46.130 --> 00:59:49.740
- And what do I have to do with that? - You know what you want.

00:59:49.780 --> 00:59:56.880
- I took all the money. - All that's missing is the piano quota.

00:59:56.890 --> 01:00:00.000
- What piano? - The one you're using. And I paid for it.

01:00:00.090 --> 01:00:01.690
but his savings ran out.

01:00:01.890 --> 01:00:04.350
Oh, God.

01:00:11.110 --> 01:00:15.060
During the four years he lived here, his behavior was exemplary.

01:00:15.260 --> 01:00:18.080
Why insist if these people don't understand anything?

01:00:18.280 --> 01:00:20.680
The institution considers that it has not been well taken care of

01:00:20.880 --> 01:00:23.280
and we have no choice but to take her away from here.

01:00:23.370 --> 01:00:24.940
And take her back to the asylum?

01:00:25.140 --> 01:00:27.540
There she will learn what you did not teach her.

01:00:27.790 --> 01:00:29.600
You can go and look for your things,

01:01:28.730 --> 01:01:30.000
Why didn't you tell me it was Lucía?

01:01:30.000 --> 01:01:32.840
- The one who gave you the ring. - Because I'm a liar.

01:01:32.840 --> 01:01:37.360
She also told me you paid the piano. With your savings.

01:01:37.360 --> 01:01:41.300
What nonsense! You can't trust anyone's secret.

01:01:41.300 --> 01:01:45.260
Clarita, you have to forgive me. I've lived without realizing it.

01:01:45.260 --> 01:01:48.260
You're the best creature in the world.

01:01:48.260 --> 01:01:52.430
- I'm nothing. Don't exaggerate things. - Yes, you're a man.

01:01:52.430 --> 01:01:56.330
I swear I'll ever be able to pay you for all this you've done for me.

01:01:56.330 --> 01:02:00.000
It's not worth it. I have to go.

01:02:01.340 --> 01:02:04.070
- I'll be waiting downstairs. - I love you.

01:02:04.260 --> 01:02:15.080
- I've always loved you. - Your eyes...

01:04:41.000 --> 01:04:44.960
- I'm leaving. - You're on tour.

01:04:45.160 --> 01:04:53.930
- So you can't keep working. - Don't lie to me.

01:04:54.130 --> 01:05:00.000
It's fine. I just wanted to ask you for a favor.

01:05:00.760 --> 01:05:03.840
- Tell me, Mom. - Don't tell anyone, really.

01:05:04.660 --> 01:05:13.960
- It would be a shame. - Don't worry.

01:07:59.630 --> 01:08:00.000
How are you?

01:08:02.270 --> 01:08:04.870
I came to look for you. Canaro got sick.

01:08:04.930 --> 01:08:08.090
- Are you willing to replace him? - Of course. I'd love to.

01:08:08.370 --> 01:08:11.050
- What were you playing? - A tango.

01:08:11.110 --> 01:08:13.670
- Yours? - Yes, I just got it.

01:08:13.700 --> 01:08:18.980
- You're talented. - No one has noticed yet.

01:08:19.110 --> 01:08:21.760
The Club Progreso Alegria de Caballito is tomorrow.

01:08:21.830 --> 01:08:23.730
- We have to dance. - Okay.

01:08:23.920 --> 01:08:27.840
- Are you staying? - We're going out.

01:09:00.800 --> 01:09:16.550
I will never be well again, maybe you will wait for me over there.

01:09:30.190 --> 01:09:32.430
- See you tomorrow. - You're not coming with me, Vinoto?

01:09:32.510 --> 01:09:35.250
- I'll take you. - Master, why don't you listen to the kid?

01:09:35.510 --> 01:09:38.180
Look, I'm in a hurry now. Maybe another time.

01:09:38.260 --> 01:09:39.680
Listen to him, it's worth it.

01:09:39.770 --> 01:09:42.430
- Do you think so? - Yes, Master. This boy is talented.

01:09:42.810 --> 01:09:47.020
Well, look, what are you going to play?

01:09:47.450 --> 01:09:51.120
- A tango that I composed. - Well, just play it.

01:09:51.450 --> 01:09:52.630
- Sure. - Thank you very much.

01:11:10.720 --> 01:11:11.240
We'll be right back.

01:12:16.480 --> 01:12:28.130
Oh, money. I think what you

01:12:30.990 --> 01:12:35.540
Roman, you...

01:13:31.940 --> 01:13:32.240
Oh!

01:14:35.500 --> 01:14:38.470
I know she really did it, because she's so sure.

01:14:39.190 --> 01:14:40.630
That's what Delfino told her.

01:14:41.430 --> 01:14:44.310
Music triumphs when a little organ takes it around the neighborhood.

01:14:45.310 --> 01:14:46.670
And will she look for you again?

01:14:48.220 --> 01:14:50.960
- Will those who triumph come back? - Clarita.

01:15:00.320 --> 01:15:00.960
Oh, my God.
